Only `lib/` and `test/` have an owner. The root files and `.github/` have none, because nobody holds half of the surviving lines.

I did not use the busfactor script's output. It weights commits by age, and it counted the formatter commit and named Fiona Formatter as a fallback owner. I measured with `git blame` at HEAD instead. The blame run ignored the reformat commit `62628c0`, ignored whitespace changes, and followed moved lines. I excluded dependabot lines and merged Troy Goode's two emails into one person. The percentages are each person's share of the non-bot lines.

| Path | Top holder | Share | Next | Result |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `lib/` | Troy Goode | 67% | Douglas Wilson 9% | owner |
| `test/` | Troy Goode | 54% | Douglas Wilson 39% | owner |
| `.github/` | Douglas Wilson | 32% | Íñigo Marquínez Prado 26% | no owner |
| root files | Troy Goode | 32% | Douglas Wilson 28% | no owner |

The root files are `.eslintrc.yml`, `.gitignore`, `HISTORY.md`, `LICENSE`, `README.md` and `package.json`.

Suggested lines:

```
# lib/ and test/: one person holds at least half of the surviving lines
/lib/   <email redacted>
/test/  <email redacted>

# .github/ and root files: no one holds half, so no owner is named
```

- **Handle:** I used Troy's git email because I did not look up GitHub handles. Replace it with their `@handle` before committing.
- **`test/` margin:** 54% is close to the cutoff. Troy's two newest commits (`b2005d9`, `02afce3`) are in his count, and I did not check how many lines they account for.
- **Troy's two emails:** I merged `<email redacted>` and `troy@laptop.example` because the author name matches. Both emails are treated as the same person.
- **Activity:** I did not check whether Troy is still active. Confirm that before making them the only owner.

