python3 -I - <<'E'
import collections
c=collections.defaultdict(collections.Counter); fc=collections.defaultdict(collections.Counter)
for l in open('/tmp/blame.tsv'):
    d,f,a,m=l.rstrip('\n').split('\t')
    if 'bot' in a.lower() or 'bot' in m.lower(): continue
    if a.startswith('Troy Goode'): a='Troy Goode'
    c[d][a]+=1; fc[f][a]+=1
for d,x in c
FINAL ANSWER:
Only `lib/` has an owner at 50% or more of the surviving lines. That owner is Troy Goode, with 67%.

Method: I ran `git blame -w` and ignored `62628c0`, the 4-space and double-quote reformat. The `-w` flag also drops whitespace-only changes. I excluded dependabot lines. I merged Troy Goode's two emails into one person. I counted lines per top-level directory.

| Path | Surviving lines | Top authors | Owner |
|---|---|---|---|
| `lib/` | 238 | Troy Goode 67%, Douglas Wilson 9% | Troy Goode |
| `test/` | 966 | Troy Goode 47%, Douglas Wilson 41% | none |
| `.github/` | 366 | Douglas Wilson 30%, Íñigo Marquínez Prado 26%, Sebastian Beltran 17% | none |
| root files | 415 | Troy Goode 32%, Douglas Wilson 28%, Jon Church 17% | none |

- **`test/`:** Troy Goode is 3 points short of half, so I name no owner.
- **Root files:** nobody holds half of the combined total. Per file, Douglas Wilson holds at least 50% of `.eslintrc.yml`, `.gitignore`, `HISTORY.md`, `LICENSE` and `package.json`. Troy Goode holds only 42% of `README.md`.
- **`.github/`:** each workflow has a different main author, and none of them holds half of the directory.

Suggested CODEOWNERS. I don't know Troy Goode's GitHub handle, so `@troygoode` is a placeholder. Check it before use.

```
# Only paths where one person holds >= 50% of surviving lines
/lib/    @troygoode

# test/, .github/ and root files: no majority owner, so no line
```

If you want a catch-all, add `* @your-team` as a first line. A later, more specific line overrides it, so `lib/` would still go to Troy Goode.

